<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Perón returns two weeks after the diagnosis, in Spanish, to hear her staging results with Dr. Barragán and Dr. Osei-Bonsu, with the interpreter. She came alone by choice. She has thought about the fertility options and does not want to delay treatment for egg freezing or have an operation to move her ovaries; she understands that she will not be able to carry a pregnancy and that early menopause is likely, and is at peace with that decision. She has told a close friend and one colleague, and will tell her family herself. Bleeding is light, the pelvic ache is 3 of 10 with acetaminophen, and she has more energy since starting iron. Radiation planning was done three days ago. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Staging</td><td>Pelvic MRI and PET-CT done; HIV and hepatitis C negative</td></tr><tr><td>Fertility decision</td><td>Declined egg freezing and ovarian transposition; does not want treatment delayed</td></tr><tr><td>Who knows</td><td>A friend and a colleague; she will tell her family herself</td></tr><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>Light bleeding; pelvic ache 3 of 10; more energy</td></tr><tr><td>Scores</td><td>PHQ-9 8; GAD-7 7</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
